    "q-95989": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95989",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Given that $X∼U\\{3,4,5,…,22\\},$ compute $P(X=7).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{3,4,5,…,22\\},$ and the set $S=\\{3,4,5,…,22\\}$ has $|S|=22-3+1=20$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{20}, & x=3,4,5,…,22 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(X=7)=f(7)=\\frac{1}{20}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
