      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Given that $X∼U\\{-10,-9,-8,…,5\\},$ compute $P(X=5).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{-10,-9,-8,…,5\\},$ and the set $S=\\{-10,-9,-8,…,5\\}$ has $|S|=5-(-10)+1=16$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{16}, & x=-10,-9,-8,…,5 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(X=5)=f(5)=\\frac{1}{16}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
