    "q-96811": {
      "dom_id": "step-q96811",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Given $X∼U\\{2,3,4,…,11\\},$ compute $P(X\\ge 5).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{2,3,4,…,11\\},$ and the set $S=\\{2,3,4,…,11\\}$ has $|S|=11-2+1=10$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{10}, & x=2,3,4,…,11 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $S,$ the items that satisfy $X\\ge 5$ are $5,6,7,…,11.$ There are $11-5+1=7$ of these items. Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 5)=7\\cdot \\frac{1}{10}=\\frac{7}{10}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
