      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Given $X∼U\\{5,9,12,13,14,15\\},$ compute $P(X<12).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{5,9,12,13,14,15\\},$ and the set $S=\\{5,9,12,13,14,15\\}$ has $|S|=6$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6}, & x=5,9,12,13,14,15 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $S,$ there are $2$ items $(5,9)$ that satisfy $X<12.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(X<12)=2\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$",
