    "q-96812": {
      "dom_id": "step-q96812",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Given $X∼U\\{9,10,11,…,28\\},$ compute $P(X>25).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{9,10,11,…,28\\},$ and the set $S=\\{9,10,11,…,28\\}$ has $|S|=28-9+1=20$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{20}, & x=9,10,11,…,28 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $S,$ the items that satisfy $X>25$ are $26,27,28.$ There are $3$ of these items. Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(X>25)=3\\cdot \\frac{1}{20}=\\frac{3}{20}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
