    "q-164163": {
      "dom_id": "step-q164163",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Given $X∼U\\{0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8\\},$ compute $P(2<X\\le 7).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8\\},$ and the set $S=\\{0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8\\}$ has $|S|=9$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{9}, & x=0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $S,$ there are $5$ items $(3,4,5,6,7)$ that satisfy $2<X\\le 7.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(2<X\\le 7)=5\\cdot \\frac{1}{9}=\\frac{5}{9}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
