    "q-96835": {
      "dom_id": "step-q96835",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Given $X∼U\\{1,3,5,6,8,10,12\\},$ compute $P(3<X<8).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{1,3,5,6,8,10,12\\},$ and the set $S=\\{1,3,5,6,8,10,12\\}$ has $|S|=7$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{7}, & x=1,3,5,6,8,10,12 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $S,$ there are $2$ items $(5,6)$ that satisfies $3<X<8.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(3<X<8)=2\\cdot \\frac{1}{7}=\\frac{2}{7}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
